================================================================================
WHY GPL, WHEN THIS USED TO BE MIT
================================================================================

The song recogniser in the Cortana app is a Kotlin port of the fingerprinting
half of SongRec, by marin-m, which is GPL-3.0. Shazam's signature format is
only documented inside that project, and their server accepts nothing else, so
there is no way to speak to it without building on that work. GPL-3.0 is the
price of doing so, and it is a fair one: the whole reason the recogniser could
be written at all is that somebody else published theirs.

Nothing else changed. This is the same project it was, under a licence that
asks the same of anyone forking it that its own dependency asked.


