================================================================================
SONG RECOGNITION
================================================================================

app/src/main/java/rocks/gorjan/gokixp/apps/cortana/shazam/

    Ported from SongRec by marin-m, GPL-3.0.
    https://github.com/marin-m/SongRec

    Specifically `src/core/fingerprinting/` - the signature generator, the
    binary signature format, and the shape of the request their server expects.
    The Kotlin is written from scratch, including a real-input FFT that SongRec
    takes from a crate and a Hann window it ships as a table; the algorithm,
    its constants and the wire format are theirs.

    SongRec's own README notes that the technique is covered by patents in some
    jurisdictions outside the EU. Shazam's foundational patent (Wang et al.,
    US 6,990,453, filed 2000) has since expired.

    No audio leaves the phone. What is sent is the fingerprint - a list of
    (time, frequency, magnitude) peaks - from which the recording cannot be
    reconstructed and in which speech is not intelligible.


